                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ddf14382-2c70-38f8-aa53-95d9878227d3",
                                        "entry_id": "4faa8f74-fd84-3093-aa5a-bdc5da0445d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Members of genus Oxalis or family Oxalidaceae, woodsorrels."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79c82196-4273-3ca1-9ee2-709ec87d330e",
                                        "entry_id": "4faa8f74-fd84-3093-aa5a-bdc5da0445d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The roselle, Hibiscus sabdariffa."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5c274cb5-cce2-3699-b950-542ad4370681",
                                        "entry_id": "4faa8f74-fd84-3093-aa5a-bdc5da0445d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The roselle, Hibiscus sabdariffa.",
                                            "A drink, consumed especially in the Caribbean around Christmas, made from the flowers of Hibiscus sabdariffa: hibiscus tea."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b182edae-dd3a-4a53-8ace-6f58f1b763bf",
                                                "sense_id": "5c274cb5-cce2-3699-b950-542ad4370681",
                                                "text": "Now, many people drink alcohol, but when I was a child I remember drinking sorrel, ginger beer and drinks made from fresh fruits such as soursop and passion-fruit. Sorrel was prepared over a long period, not as quickly as it is now."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2988c8e9-c361-41c7-8eb8-4ac28d240dd5",
                                                "sense_id": "5c274cb5-cce2-3699-b950-542ad4370681",
                                                "text": "For instance, one day we were sitting on the porch, looking down at the lagoon and the yachts from all over the world. He was drinking ginger beer mixed with rum, and I was drinking sorrel. No rum. Out of nowhere, he proposed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b422b13e-78a3-4b99-9869-119bf3460a9e",
                                                "sense_id": "5c274cb5-cce2-3699-b950-542ad4370681",
                                                "text": "Joy and the parents did not go either; we spent a quiet day at home, eating roast chicken and stuffing with our own green-gungu rice and peas, and drinking sorrel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sorrel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eace1f67-b5b6-3fd9-a0d2-a7b05a29808e",
                                        "entry_id": "e74764fd-4f56-3e66-a6b6-cc249a4580d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A brown colour, with a tint of red."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sorrel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e433605-809e-375b-99af-cb1bc5355b8d",
                                        "entry_id": "6837ab99-0941-36e0-a0bf-5bfd0d1a2ccf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a brown colour, with a tint of red. (especially: a sorrel horse)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22b0df5c-84fd-40e5-beab-6bee938591cf",
                                                "sense_id": "9e433605-809e-375b-99af-cb1bc5355b8d",
                                                "text": "A little harmless gossip ensued on various themes, such as where old Aunt Sally got her new red head-kerchief, and how \"Missis was a going to give Lizzy that spotted muslin gown, when she 'd got her new berage made up;\" and how Mas'r Shelby was thinking of buying a new sorrel colt, that was going to prove an addition to the glories of the place."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "207962d3-7867-48d3-82f3-b9fb32fcf5d2",
                        "source_entry_id": "7e5c8e0f-6b3f-312e-9c36-e77e46e906ad",
                        "source_sense_id": "05fc1d39-bcb8-3df2-b283-33a10d34266b",
                        "source_sense_description": "en 2. (bladeren van) de plant Rumex acetosa",
                        "target_lang_word": "oseille",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "oseille",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "77ef692e-af71-36ef-a6db-ab13db324587",
                                        "entry_id": "1cbac649-ef5c-3506-b558-406ff91c6deb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Plante potagère de la famille des Polygonacées d’un goût acide."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce8da5af-614a-461c-a7fe-f87bab451862",
                                                "sense_id": "77ef692e-af71-36ef-a6db-ab13db324587",
                                                "text": "Les diverses espèces d’oseille semblent avoir, dès l’origine, poussé spontanément en Europe. Puis les Anciens les ont cultivées pour leur usage culinaire et c’est surtout à partir du XIVᵉ siècle qu’on les trouve à la base de nombreuses sauces."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "919a5853-a063-4572-8813-e952bebb0ed6",
                                                "sense_id": "77ef692e-af71-36ef-a6db-ab13db324587",
                                                "text": "Le saumon et l’oseille font un mariage classique, mais en papillote, c’est plus original !"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c944091-000a-4bf4-9d73-ed567bb40864",
                                                "sense_id": "77ef692e-af71-36ef-a6db-ab13db324587",
                                                "text": "Lantier paraissait ne pas comprendre, mangeait lentement du veau à l’oseille."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75fbac0f-c302-47cb-89c2-7331ac8e5b3a",
                                                "sense_id": "77ef692e-af71-36ef-a6db-ab13db324587",
                                                "text": "Aux environs de Paris, on sème l’oseille au printemps."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "612ee922-ad03-3b35-94cd-0f9d670b6eca",
                                        "entry_id": "1cbac649-ef5c-3506-b558-406ff91c6deb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Argent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12097f63-67d6-4be2-9efa-7ae14822a5f7",
                                                "sense_id": "612ee922-ad03-3b35-94cd-0f9d670b6eca",
                                                "text": "Une nénette enceinte, c’est pas l’Himalaya, et un contrôle fiscal, c’est pas un mardi noir à Wall Street. D’abord tu largues la nénette, je te file l’oseille en liquide pour les formalités. Ensuite, tu disparais du bureau, […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b63873a-32f6-4dac-97cb-8bcc8358f8b8",
                                                "sense_id": "612ee922-ad03-3b35-94cd-0f9d670b6eca",
                                                "text": "En fait, il se trouvait beaucoup plus d’affinités avec Job, qui était davantage un homme de son style et de son monde, un type on ne peut plus respectable, plein d’oseille et tout."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9e973d3-5cba-4484-a811-7a219a7fedcf",
                                                "sense_id": "612ee922-ad03-3b35-94cd-0f9d670b6eca",
                                                "text": "Il a toujours eu horreur des pâtes, ce qui est un handicap certain quand on n’a pas d’oseille (ne pas écrire quand on a l’estomac vide : ça influence le style)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e53f7df-fa98-495f-b5b5-f43a6c78cf78",
                                                "sense_id": "612ee922-ad03-3b35-94cd-0f9d670b6eca",
                                                "text": "Dans les banques, y a pas qu’ de l’oseille\nY a des employés qui font leur métier\nEt c’est bien comm’ c’est."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73c031e9-881c-4ffd-bd3b-9df76202ce85",
                                                "sense_id": "612ee922-ad03-3b35-94cd-0f9d670b6eca",
                                                "text": "(…) les mecs qui vont à Davos, ce sont ceux qui ont de l’oseille."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "543bb5e8-b07b-488c-9c8c-0093b0382660",
                        "source_entry_id": "7e5c8e0f-6b3f-312e-9c36-e77e46e906ad",
